# Miner Llama v5 preset (in progress): Ornith-1.5-122B, Ornith-1.5-122B Pascal N2P GGUF (valid1: N2P/N3P experts, Q5_0
# output layer) on nine P106-090 cards, 49,152-token context.
# Build: the v5 engine, pascal-p106-v5 at 602691153 or later (upstream b12483 merged). v4.0's engine does not read the
# switch below, so this file needs the v5 engine; on v4.0 use release/ornith-v4/settings.env.
# This is v4.0's preset (release/ornith-v4/settings.env, explained in release/ornith-v4/README.md) with one switch
# added, GGML_CUDA_MMID_GLU_UNFUSE=2. On the coding-agent check, two runs with it against two without on the same engine
# and rig: every task passed in all four, a decode step 6.3 % shorter (57.22 and 57.70 ms against 61.26 and 61.35 ms at
# the same mix of contexts), a task at equal work 6.6 % shorter (2.04 and 2.05 minutes against 2.17 and 2.21), prompt
# reading the same (docs/data/2026-11-18_r204_ornith_glu_agent/). On the deep lane every reply is the same bytes with
# and without it (docs/data/2026-11-18_c865b_ornith_glu_rig1/).
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
PRESET_MODEL=Ornith-1.5-122B-N2P-N3P-valid1-headQ5_0.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE=decode"  # v3.0's: a one-thread block per card holds the boost clock while a split decodes; 16.3 against 14.9 tok/s (Q1021, Q1045)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE_EAGER=1"  # the keep-alive block ends before a kernel's first launch on a card, so the launch does not wait ~1 s for it; a 2,760-token prompt 24,712.63 and 24,744.13 ms against 26,637.95 and 26,065.24 without (C811, C817, Q1417, Q1426; R140, on Flash-Next)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2"  # a step's yield to the server's reader thread wakes it only when a read waits, the same replies (C741, Q1310; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1"  # the card's sampling chain (-bs, top-k 20) runs one top-k over its output rows and reads the logits unpadded, the same tokens (C691, Q1223; R83; the graph fixed by C802, Q1406)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_HOP_STAGED=1"  # each hop between cards through a pinned host ring; the same replies (FN93b); part of the prompt stack (R162, R166)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS_FORCE=1"  # prompt micro-batches captured as CUDA graphs without the two-call warm-up; the same replies (FN93b)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMID_GLU_UNFUSE=2"  # no fused matrix-vector launch on Pascal (upstream's #32239): the fused products of batches of at most 8 tokens, Ornith's gate and up among them, run as plain launches, which a P106 runs faster; a decode step 6.3 % shorter on the agent check, prompts unchanged, the same replies (C865, C865b, R204; Q1559, Q1593)
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

# v4.0's line, unchanged (release/ornith-v4/settings.env):
PRESET_ARGS="-ngl 99 -fa on -c 49152 -np 1 -bs --ctx-checkpoints 4 --cache-ram 0 --jinja --reasoning-format deepseek --temp 0.6 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 -b 4096 -ub 512 -ts 6,6,6,6,5,5,5,5,6 -fit off"
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-vram 4"  # a slot's newest four checkpoints of the Gated DeltaNet state on the cards, not in host memory; the same replies (FN93b)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-incall"  # checkpoints taken inside a prompt's call instead of cutting the call; the same replies (FN93b)

# Opt-in, not in the preset: the micro-batch taper (release/ornith-v4/settings.env explains it). To turn it on:
#   PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ubatch-taper short=600:64"
